  cybertrain generate job NAME [--retry Klass:wait:attempts ...] [--force]
      Add a background job: app/jobs/NAME_job.rb (a Cybertrain::Job::Base
      with an empty perform(args) and a retry_on line per --retry: wait
      in seconds or polynomially_longer, then the attempts) and a test
      running it. Queue it with NameJob.perform_later("id" => 1) once
      `spin run gen` has written gen/jobs.rb.
  cybertrain db migrate
      Generate, apply pending migrations, generate again
      (SPIN_DEBUG=1 spin run gen; SPIN_DEBUG=1 spin run db -- migrate;
      SPIN_DEBUG=1 spin run gen).
  cybertrain db COMMAND...
      Any other database command, after `SPIN_DEBUG=1 spin run gen`:
      status, rollback [N] (generates again afterwards), schema,
      schema:dump, create.
      `cybertrain migration` is the same as `cybertrain db migrate`.
  cybertrain server [PORT]
      Generate, then start the development server
      (SPIN_DEBUG=1 spin run gen; spin build NAME -- --incremental
      when a Ruby file is newer than build/bin/NAME; spin run NAME
      [-- PORT]; default port 3000).
  cybertrain build
      Build NAME with app/views embedded and assemble dist/
      (the binary, public/, storage/, tmp/).
  cybertrain test [FILE|DIR ...] [-n NAME|-n /TEXT/]
      Run the application's tests (test/**/*_test.rb and test/*.rb)
      as one program: SPIN_DEBUG=1 spin run gen, then gen/tests.rb compiled into
      build/test/tests when a source is newer than it, then run.
      FILE or DIR keeps the tests of those files; -n NAME the test
      named NAME (or its method name, test_...); -n /TEXT/ the tests
      whose name contains TEXT. A filter never recompiles. Exits 1
      when a test failed, 2 for bad arguments.
  cybertrain spin ARGS...
      Run spin with the pinned Spinel, from any directory
      (cybertrain spin test; cybertrain spin run gen -- --check).
  cybertrain secret [--hex]
      Print a new random secret for CYBERTRAIN_SECRET_KEY_BASE (signs
      the session cookie); with --hex, a new key for
      CYBERTRAIN_ENCRYPTION_KEY (encrypts the columns of `encrypts`).
      Both are 64 hex digits (32 random bytes). Keep the encryption
      key: data encrypted with it cannot be read without it.
  cybertrain setup [--force]
      Install Spinel 2026.11.04.7026 into ~/.cybertrain (CYBERTRAIN_HOME)
      unless a spinel of that release is already on PATH, and print
      the PATH line for ~/.cybertrain/bin. The commands above do the
      install by themselves the first time they need spin.
  cybertrain doctor
      Check the C toolchain, the SQLite headers and the Spinel install.
  cybertrain version
  cybertrain help
ok   CLI version, help and unknown commands
# The secrets this application reads from its environment. This file
# is committed: copy a line into the environment (or your deploy's
# secrets) with a value, never write the value here.

# Signs the session cookie; changing it signs everyone out. Required in
# production; development and test keep one in tmp/secret_key.
# Make one with `cybertrain secret`.
# CYBERTRAIN_SECRET_KEY_BASE=

# Encrypts the columns a model declares with `encrypts`; boot fails
# without it once one does. Keep it safe: encrypted data cannot be
# read without it. To rotate, move the old key to
# CYBERTRAIN_ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS (comma-separated) and re-save.
# CYBERTRAIN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=  # cybertrain secret --hex

# Settings, not secrets. /up answers 503 "feed stale" once a
# WebSocket feed has stopped reporting; 0 turns that check off.
# CYBERTRAIN_HEALTH_FEEDS=0
# Seconds of silence after which a feed counts as stale (180).
# CYBERTRAIN_HEALTH_FEED_STALE=180

# The application's time zone (an IANA name; UTC when unset): the
# boundaries of today and this week, Date.current, l and time_tag.
# CYBERTRAIN_TIME_ZONE=Asia/Tokyo
# The IANA zone cron expressions are read in; the time zone above
# when unset.
# CYBERTRAIN_SCHEDULER_TZ=Asia/Tokyo

# Redirect http to https and mark cookies Secure (production behind
# a TLS-terminating proxy).
# CYBERTRAIN_FORCE_SSL=1
# The host names the application answers to, comma-separated.
# CYBERTRAIN_HOSTS=app.example.com

# Logs and error reports. Settings, except the DSN, which is kept out of the repository like a secret.
# The least important log line written: debug, info, warn, error or
# none (info).
# CYBERTRAIN_LOG_LEVEL=info
# How each line is written: text (the default) or json, one JSON
# object per line, for a log collector.
# CYBERTRAIN_LOG_FORMAT=json
# Where error reports are sent, a Sentry DSN; empty sends nothing.
# It holds a key: set it in the environment (or your deploy's
# secrets), never in a file you commit. It needs
# require "cybertrain/error_reporter/sentry" in bin/<app>.rb.
# CYBERTRAIN_SENTRY_DSN=https://<public key>@<host>/<project id>
# The share of error reports sent, 0.0 to 1.0 (1.0, all of them).
# CYBERTRAIN_ERROR_SAMPLE_RATE=1.0
# The release sent with each error report: a version or a commit.
# CYBERTRAIN_RELEASE=
ok   .env.example lists the secrets, commented, with how to make each
ok   new writes the logging and reporting variables, all commented
